- # `↯/s.123.2` — `Git.RefError`
+ # `↯/s.123.2` — `Git.RefError`

- Raised when a value is not a valid Git reference name.
+ Se lanza cuando un valor no es un nombre de referencia de Git válido.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Octogenarian validates reference names against `git
- check-ref-format`'s rules. The constructor records the offending
- `value` and a `reason: Reason`; the rendered message is `$value
- is not a valid Git reference because $reason`.
+ Octogenarian valida los nombres de referencia según las reglas de `git check-ref-format`. El
+ constructor registra el `value` problemático y un `reason: Reason`; el mensaje representado es
+ `$value is not a valid Git reference because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.123.2.1`  `LeadingOrTrailingDot`  A path segment of the reference starts or ends with `.`.  `[↯/s.123.2.1] .verona is not a valid Git reference because a path segment starts or ends with .`  Trim the leading or trailing dot from the segment.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.2`  `ReservedSuffix`  A path segment matches `*.lock`, a pattern which Git reserves for lock files.  `[↯/s.123.2.2] feature.lock is not a valid Git reference because a path segment ends with the reserved suffix .lock`  Choose a name which does not match `*.lock`.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.3`  `ReservedSequence`  The name contains `@{`, which Git reserves for reflog selectors (e.g. `HEAD@{1}`).  `[↯/s.123.2.3] verona@{capulet} is not a valid Git reference because the name contains the reserved sequence @{`  Remove or replace the `@{` sequence.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.4`  `DoubleDot`  The name contains `..`, which Git reserves for range selectors.  `[↯/s.123.2.4] verona..capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains ..`  Replace the `..` with a single `.` or another separator.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.5`  `EmptySegment`  The name contains an empty path segment — typically a leading, trailing, or doubled `/`.  `[↯/s.123.2.5] verona//capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains an empty path segment`  Remove the empty segment.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.6`  `InvalidCharacter`  The name contains a character Git forbids in references: any of `*`, `[`, `\`, ` `, `^`, `~`, `:`, or `?`.  `[↯/s.123.2.6] verona capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains a character forbidden by Git`  Replace the forbidden character with `-` or `_`.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.7`  `BadHash`  The value passed to `Git.Hash` was not a 40-character lowercase hexadecimal string.  `[↯/s.123.2.7] abc is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a 40-character hexadecimal hash`  Provide the full 40-character SHA-1 commit hash.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.8`  `BadRefspec`  The value passed to `Git.Refspec.parse` was not a refspec: it had more than one `:` separating source and destination.  `[↯/s.123.2.8] a:b:c is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a valid refspec`  Write the refspec as `source`, `source:destination` or `:destination`, with an optional leading `+`.
+ column  Código
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significado
+ column  Mensaje
+ column  Solución
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.1`  `LeadingOrTrailingDot`  Un segmento de ruta de la referencia empieza o termina por `.`.  `[↯/s.123.2.1] .verona is not a valid Git reference because a path segment starts or ends with .`  Quita el punto inicial o final del segmento.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.2`  `ReservedSuffix`  Un segmento de ruta coincide con `*.lock`, un patrón que Git reserva para los ficheros de bloqueo.  `[↯/s.123.2.2] feature.lock is not a valid Git reference because a path segment ends with the reserved suffix .lock`  Elige un nombre que no coincida con `*.lock`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.3`  `ReservedSequence`  El nombre contiene `@{`, que Git reserva para los selectores del reflog (p. ej., `HEAD@{1}`).  `[↯/s.123.2.3] verona@{capulet} is not a valid Git reference because the name contains the reserved sequence @{`  Elimina o sustituye la secuencia `@{`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.4`  `DoubleDot`  El nombre contiene `..`, que Git reserva para los selectores de rango.  `[↯/s.123.2.4] verona..capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains ..`  Sustituye el `..` por un solo `.` o por otro separador.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.5`  `EmptySegment`  El nombre contiene un segmento de ruta vacío, normalmente una `/` inicial, final o duplicada.  `[↯/s.123.2.5] verona//capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains an empty path segment`  Elimina el segmento vacío.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.6`  `InvalidCharacter`  El nombre contiene un carácter que Git prohíbe en las referencias: cualquiera de `*`, `[`, `\`, ` `, `^`, `~`, `:` o `?`.  `[↯/s.123.2.6] verona capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains a character forbidden by Git`  Sustituye el carácter prohibido por `-` o `_`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.7`  `BadHash`  El valor pasado a `Git.Hash` no era una cadena hexadecimal en minúsculas de 40 caracteres.  `[↯/s.123.2.7] abc is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a 40-character hexadecimal hash`  Proporciona el hash SHA-1 completo de 40 caracteres del commit.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.8`  `BadRefspec`  El valor pasado a `Git.Refspec.parse` no era un refspec: tenía más de un `:` separando el origen y el destino.  `[↯/s.123.2.8] a:b:c is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a valid refspec`  Escribe el refspec como `source`, `source:destination` o `:destination`, con un `+` inicial opcional.

